// # oodar/docs/CAPABILITIES_TABLE.oot — Full Cap Token Inventory (26 substrate caps, 20 NORTHSTAR language tokens)
//
// Logline: Every cap token in v4.5.0 is enumerated here with its NORTHSTAR language class (core vs hardware-only future-state), bit position, grant function, require function, attenuation function, and the consuming oo_* symbols — a single table that maps sec/cap/caps.h to the call sites in the rest of the runtime.
//
// Setup: This is the canonical reference for the cap model. It is cross-referenced with sec/cap/caps.h, sec/cap/ANCHOR.oo, and the bridge (oodar/sec/cap/cap_ocap_bridge.c). The 4 reserved/dead bit positions (HITL/SYNC/MEM/HTTP at bits 13-16) are not tokens — they are gap reservations; see docs/SECURITY_MODEL.oot Beat 2 for the rationale.
//
// Beats:
//   1. NORTHSTAR language caps (20 tokens — FsReadCap..CompilerReadCap).
//   2. Hardware-only future-state caps (6 tokens — Audio/Camera/Usb/Hid/Window/Frame).
//   3. The 4 reserved/dead bit positions.
//   4. How to read the table.

# === How to read the table ===

// Each row gives:
//   - Name         : the human-readable cap name
//   - Bit          : the OODAR_CAP_<NAME> bit position
//   - Class        : NORTHSTAR language (granted AND required AND has consumer)
//                    or hardware-only future-state (no NORTHSTAR language
//                    token yet — bridge maps to FsReadCap)
//   - Grant        : the oo_cap_grant_<name> function in sec/cap/caps.c
//   - Require      : the oo_cap_require_<name> function in sec/cap/cap_require.c
//                    (and cap_alloc.c / cap_time.c / cap_ffi.c for the
//                    sub-store caps; see sec/cap/ANCHOR.oo for the inventory)
//   - Attenuate    : the oo_cap_attenuate function in sec/cap/cap.c
//                    (applies to all caps via the bitmask subset check)
//   - Used by      : the oo_* call sites in the runtime that require
//                    this cap, with file:line references
//
// The oo_cap_attenuate function takes a parent_hmac and a child_rights
// bitmask. It is the only cap-derivation path; the child can never
// gain rights the parent did not have. Attenuation is generic —
// the same function works for all 26 tokens.

# === Beat 1: NORTHSTAR language caps (20 tokens — FsReadCap..CompilerReadCap) ===

// =====================================================================
// Name            | Bit | Class     | Grant                  | Require
// =====================================================================
// FsRead          |  3  | core      | oo_cap_grant_fsread    | oo_cap_require_fsread
// FsWrite         |  2  | core      | oo_cap_grant_fswrite   | oo_cap_require_fswrite
// Net             |  0  | core      | oo_cap_grant_net       | oo_cap_require_net
// Tcp             | 17  | core      | oo_cap_grant_tcp       | oo_cap_require_tcp
// Udp             | 18  | core      | oo_cap_grant_udp       | oo_cap_require_udp
// Sys             |  4  | core      | oo_cap_grant_sys       | oo_cap_require_sys
// Process         |  1  | core      | oo_cap_grant_process   | oo_cap_require_process
// Env             | 28  | core      | oo_cap_grant_env       | oo_cap_require_env
// Time            |  6  | core      | oo_cap_grant_time      | oo_cap_require_time
// Rand            |  7  | core      | oo_cap_grant_rand      | oo_cap_require_rand
// Alloc           |  8  | core      | oo_cap_grant_alloc     | oo_cap_require_alloc
// Thread          | 26  | core      | oo_cap_grant_thread    | oo_cap_require_thread
// Gpu             | 27  | core      | oo_cap_grant_gpu       | oo_cap_require_gpu
// Ffi             | 10  | core      | oo_cap_grant_ffi       | oo_cap_require_ffi
// Fs              |  5  | core      | oo_cap_grant_fs        | oo_cap_require_fs
// Arena           |  9  | core      | oo_cap_grant_arena     | oo_cap_require_arena
// Metrics         | 11  | core      | oo_cap_grant_metrics   | oo_cap_require_metrics
// Sign            | 12  | core      | oo_cap_grant_sign      | oo_cap_require_sign
// Bind            | 19  | core      | oo_cap_grant_bind      | oo_cap_require_bind
// CompilerRead    | 29  | core      | oo_cap_grant_compiler_read | oo_cap_require_compiler_read
// =====================================================================
// All 20 NORTHSTAR language tokens are granted + required + have a real
// consumer. The 22 oo_cap_require_* gates in sec/cap/cap_require.c
// (plus 4 sub-store require fns in cap_alloc.c / cap_time.c / cap_ffi.c
// — alloc/time/rand/ffi — for a total of 26 substrate caps covered)
// exhaust the 26-token substrate set. The bridge
// (cap_ocap_bridge.c: SUBSTRATE_TO_LANGUAGE[26]) maps every substrate
// cap to one of the 20 NORTHSTAR language tokens. The hardware-only
// substrate caps (audio/camera/usb/hid/window/frame) map to FsReadCap
// as a placeholder — see Beat 2.
//
// Fs is the umbrella FS cap (rights_mask=31, full authority). It is
// granted+required in v4.5.0 and is the alias for FsRead+FsWrite
// (oo_cap_require_fsread accepts g_tok_fsread OR g_tok_fs;
// oo_cap_require_fswrite accepts g_tok_fswrite OR g_tok_fs). The
// v4.3.0+ bridge treats FsCap as a real language token (rights=31),
// not a legacy placeholder.
//
// BindCap is granted+required and consumed by oo_bind_udp
// (alias for NetCap/TcpCap). It is a NORTHSTAR language token
// (BindCap), not a future-state hardware placeholder.
//
// Used by (NORTHSTAR language caps, by token):
//   FsRead       : fs/os/fs.c (oo_read_file, oo_path_exists, oo_file_size,
//                                oo_fs_read_dir, oo_fs_is_dir)
//   FsWrite      : fs/os/fs.c (oo_write_file, oo_fs_remove_file, oo_fs_rmdir,
//                                oo_fs_mkdir, oo_fs_hardlink, oo_fs_symlink)
//   Fs           : alias gate for fsread/fswrite; also consumed by
//                  oo_cap_require_fs as a direct gate (v4.5.0+)
//   Net          : net/fetch.c (oo_fetch), sec/landlock/sandbox.c
//                                (oo_sandbox_note_net, oo_sandbox_apply_matrix)
//   Tcp          : net/tls.c (oo_tls_connect), net/tls.c (oo_tcp_*)
//   Udp          : net/tls.c (oo_udp_*, oo_bind_udp)
//   Bind         : net/tls.c (oo_bind_udp, alias for Tcp/Net)
//   Sys          : fs/os/sys.c (oo_sys_exec, oo_process_policy_getenv),
//                  sec/landlock/proc_mem.c (oo_proc_mem_read)
//   Process      : app/xlang/xlang.c (oo_lto_xlang_link)
//   Env          : fs/os/sys.c (oo_env_get)
//   Time         : fs/os/time_rand.c (oo_time_*, oo_now_*) — moved
//                  to sec/cap/cap_time.c in v3.4.0
//   Rand         : fs/os/time_rand.c (oo_random_bytes) — moved to
//                  sec/cap/cap_time.c in v3.4.0
//   Alloc        : core/mem/alloc.c, core/mem/arena.c, core/mem/weak.c —
//                  moved to sec/cap/cap_alloc.c in v3.4.0
//   Thread       : app/actor/thread.c, app/actor/channel.c,
//                  app/actor/actor.c (oo_actor_spawn et al.)
//   Gpu          : hw/gpu/gpu.c, hw/gpu/gpu_hip.c, hw/gpu/gpu/gpu_hip_dispatch_buf.c
//   Ffi          : app/xlang/ffi.c (oo_dlopen, oo_dlsym, oo_dlclose),
//                  app/xlang/xlang.c (oo_xlang_import_c),
//                  fs/os/host.c (oo_host_build, oo_host_ast_dump, etc.) —
//                  moved to sec/cap/cap_ffi.c in v3.4.0
//   Arena        : core/mem/arena.c (oo_arena_create, oo_arena_alloc,
//                                    oo_arena_reset, oo_arena_destroy)
//   Metrics      : core/event/metrics.c (oo_metrics_incr, oo_metrics_get,
//                                         oo_metrics_reset, oo_metrics_export)
//   Sign         : app/actor/actor.c (oo_cap_rpc_send, oo_cap_rpc_recv)
//   CompilerRead : fs/os/host.c (oo_host_ast_dump, oo_host_check,
//                                  oo_host_token_dump)

# === Beat 2: Hardware-only future-state caps (6 tokens) ===

// =====================================================================
// Name            | Bit | Class        | Grant
// =====================================================================
// Audio           | 20  | future-state | oo_cap_grant_audio
// Camera          | 21  | future-state | oo_cap_grant_camera
// Usb             | 22  | future-state | oo_cap_grant_usb
// Hid             | 23  | future-state | oo_cap_grant_hid
// Window          | 24  | future-state | oo_cap_grant_window
// Frame           | 25  | future-state | oo_cap_grant_frame
// =====================================================================
// 6 hardware-only future-state tokens (no NORTHSTAR language token yet).
// Future-state caps:
//   - Have a grant function in sec/cap/caps.c.
//   - Have a require function in sec/cap/cap_require.c.
//   - Have NO real consumer in the current runtime.
//   - The bridge (cap_ocap_bridge.c: SUBSTRATE_TO_LANGUAGE) maps each
//     to FsReadCap as a placeholder so oo_cap_require_audio / camera /
//     usb / hid / window / frame still pass the OCap cross-check.
//
// The 6 hardware tokens are the wire-up points for the hw/ backend
// (audio device capture, camera frame buffer, USB HID, display window /
// compositor). The cap system is ready; the consumer code is not yet
// written. Future-state tokens must be granted only by code that has a
// concrete plan to consume them; granting without a consumer is the
// v2.0.0 mistake (AUDIT, HITL, SYNC, MEM, HTTP were granted without a
// consumer; v2.1.0 deleted them).

# === Beat 3: The 4 reserved/dead bit positions ===

// =====================================================================
// Bit Position | Former Name | Reason Removed      | v2.1.0 Status
// =====================================================================
// 0x2000       | OODAR_CAP_HITL   | declared but never defined | RESERVED
// 0x4000       | OODAR_CAP_SYNC   | granted but never required | RESERVED
// 0x8000       | OODAR_CAP_MEM    | granted but never required | RESERVED
// 0x10000      | OODAR_CAP_HTTP   | granted but never required | RESERVED
// =====================================================================
// The 4 reserved bits are part of the 32-bit cap mask (bits 0-31).
// They MUST NOT be re-used; any future cap MUST pick a new bit position
// to avoid ABI confusion. Re-introduction of HITL/SYNC/MEM/HTTP
// requires a Floor break (v5.0.0+) per sec/cap/caps.h.
//
// (Note: AUDIT at 0x800 was deleted in v2.1.0 then re-introduced as
// METRICS at the same bit position in v3.0.0 — bit 11 is reused, not
// reserved. See caps.h:13-15 for the v3.0.0 note.)

# === Beat 4: Attenuation (all 26 tokens) ===

// Attenuation is the same function for all 26 tokens:
//
//   OoStr oo_cap_attenuate(OoStr parent_hmac, OoStr child_rights);
//
// The function takes the parent's HMAC-sealed cap and a child_rights
// bitmask; it returns the child's HMAC-sealed cap if the child_rights
// is a subset of the parent's rights. The check is:
//
//   if ((parent_rights & child_rights) != child_rights) return 0;
//
// The child can never gain rights the parent did not have. There is
// no separate "attenuate_<name>" function per token — the bitmask
// is the same shape for all 26 tokens.
//
// oo_cap_attenuate_ok(parent_hmac, child_rights) is the bool variant
// that returns 1 if attenuation succeeded and 0 otherwise. Both
// functions are declared in sec/cap/caps.h and defined in sec/cap/cap.c.

# === Cap count summary ===

// 26 active tokens:
//   20 NORTHSTAR language (granted + required + consumer; canonical
//      surface per NORTHSTAR §1.4 line 157 — "There is no 14-token map")
//    6 hardware-only future-state (granted + required; no consumer;
//      bridge maps to FsReadCap placeholder)
//
// 4 reserved/dead bit positions (0x2000 HITL, 0x4000 SYNC, 0x8000 MEM,
// 0x10000 HTTP). Plus bit 0x800 (AUDIT) was deleted then re-used as
// METRICS in v3.0.0 — not reserved.
//
// 30 cap bit positions total (26 active + 4 reserved/dead) plus bit 0
// unused (no token defined there yet).
//
// The oo_cap_grant_<name> and oo_cap_require_<name> functions are
// 1:1 with the tokens; no token is shared between two grant functions.

// ──▓▓ oodar/docs/CAPABILITIES_TABLE.oot ──▓▓──
// :: 26 active tokens (20 NORTHSTAR language + 6 hardware future-state) + 4 reserved bits ::
